# mutgap_dev_barrier_report_once: A barrier wait posts one stamp-wait report per timeout and then waits without a timeout until a stamp is signalled. Child 1 (stamp index 1) blocks on 7:1 at time 0 and is reported at 2 s, with only its own index waiting. At 3.5 s child 3, stamp index 2, blocks on 7:1 too, which signals nothing; child 2 has stamp index 7, so a report walking index 2 would find it and assert (as device_gap_barrier_timeout_report_mismatch_dies). No report runs before child 2 publishes 7:1 at about 4.75 s, releasing both, before child 3's own 2 s timeout: no death. (A wait that timed out twice and reported twice would walk index 2.)
